{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>And to your fellow's wife you shall not give your seed of lying.</b> The explanation of the wise man R. Abraham, of blessed memory, is that sexual intercourse has three parts: one for procreation; the second for healing, to relieve the body's heat; and the third for lust, which is likened to the lust of beasts. And Scripture says לזרע — that is, even the choicest of these parts — and behold, she is entirely forbidden." "<b>And the Ramban,</b> of blessed memory, explained that it was necessary to write לזרע, for had it said only לא תתן שכבתך, it would have appeared that Scripture would impose excision (karet) even for lying with her to embrace and to kiss, since in this passage it warns concerning those liable to excisions. Therefore it was necessary to specify 'lying לזרע,' to make clear that it is the act of intercourse concerning which it warns and imposes excision. End of quote." "<b>And thus</b> we learn from here that one who lies with another man's wife is liable to excision (karet), and when there are witnesses and warning, their death is by strangulation, as it is said (ibid.): ״מות יומת הנואף והנואפת״ — 'the adulterer and the adulteress shall surely be put to death.' And behold, Shlomo proclaimed in the holy spirit that one who lies with another man's wife shall not be cleared from the judgment of Gehenna, and one who touches her shall not be cleared from the punishment of the body. As he said (Proverbs 6:27–28): ״היחתה איש אש בחיקו ובגדיו לא תשרפנה, אם יהלך איש על הגחלים ורגליו לא תכוינה, כן הבא אל אשת רעהו לא ינקה כל הנוגע בה״. And the reason two parables were needed was to allude to two punishments: the punishment of the body and the punishment of the soul. The punishment of the body, for the one who touches, is what he said: 'כל הנוגע בה'; the punishment of the soul, for the one who lies with her, is what he said: 'כן הבא אל אשת רעהו.' And he likened the punishment of the body to garments, for just as the garments are burned and not the body, so the body is punished in the case of touching, not the soul; but the punishment of the soul he likened to coals, for the soul is punished in them in Gehenna. And he mentioned in the middle 'לא ינקה' — that is, he shall not be cleared from the judgment of Gehenna if he lies with her, and likewise he shall not be cleared from the punishment of the body if he touches her. And the esoteric meaning of אשת איש I have already explained above, and I will allude to it further in the portion of Naso."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:26:36.202444356Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}